# Earthenware Computer Goal

> The Earthenware Computer that selects all of its own programs from a goal.

## Purpose
Explain this named build of the self-selecting computer under the Earthenware Computer Goal title. Source: fitzyracing1/earthenwarecomputer-Goal.

## How it works (plain English)
1. Name a goal.
2. Select programs for that goal.
3. Register the selection.
4. Keep internet, browser, HTTP server, GPU awareness, and a terminal.

## Key ideas
- Earthenware Computer (the named machine)
- Goal (what the machine is for)
- Self-selection (it picks its own programs)

## The actual code
```
# source: fitzyracing1/earthenwarecomputer-Goal
goal = name_goal()
select_and_register(goal)
keep_terminal_and_net()
```

## Line-by-line translation
1. name_goal() → “say the aim”
2. select_and_register(goal) → “pick programs and write them down”
3. keep_terminal_and_net() → “stay reachable”

## Decisions the program makes
- If a goal arrives → select programs
- If the list changes → re-register

## What a person would notice
Same idea as the self-selecting computer, under the Earthenware name.

## Current status
Barrage clone.

## Next possible steps
Open the source and name a goal.
